{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4376-1","published":"2026-09-28T15:16:14Z","modified":"2026-09-29T09:15:10.896797296Z","related":["CVE-2026-25797","CVE-2026-62343","CVE-2026-62363","CVE-2026-62946","CVE-2026-64685","CVE-2026-66011","CVE-2026-86420","CVE-2026-86421","CVE-2026-86423","CVE-2026-86425","CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-25797","CVE-2026-62343","CVE-2026-62363","CVE-2026-62946","CVE-2026-64685","CVE-2026-66011","CVE-2026-86420","CVE-2026-86421","CVE-2026-86423","CVE-2026-86425","CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589"],"summary":"Security update for ImageMagick","details":"This update for ImageMagick fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-62343: heap buffer over-write in morphology operation when an invalid kernel is provided (bsc#1272575).\n- CVE-2026-62363: heap buffer over-write in fx operation (bsc#1272582).\n- CVE-2026-62946: integer overflow in JNX decoder causes heap buffer over-write when processing extremly large files on\n  32-bit builds (bsc#1272580).\n- CVE-2026-64685: heap buffer over-read in BGR decoder due to missing end-of-file check (bsc#1272953).\n- CVE-2026-66011: memory Leak when providing invalid options to the cli (bsc#1272577).\n- CVE-2026-86420: denial of Service due to memory budget exhaustion (bsc#1279696).\n- CVE-2026-86421: denial of Service via memory leak in MSL decoder (bsc#1279711).\n- CVE-2026-86423: denial of service via heap-use-after-free in PerlMagick's GetList method (bsc#1279794).\n- CVE-2026-86425: denial of Service due to heap-use-after-free vulnerability (bsc#1279797).\n- CVE-2026-93586: use-after-free in the `ImagesToBlob` method can lead to a process crash (bsc#1281912).\n- CVE-2026-93587: policy bypass in the PCD, CUBE and HALD coders can lead to extra memory allocation and a denial of\n  service (bsc#1281909).\n- CVE-2026-93588: NULL pointer dereference in the PNM coder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281910).\n- CVE-2026-93589: division-by-zero flaw in the FLIF encoder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281911).\n- GHSA-hc76-7mpc-qjqh: code injection in HTML encoder due to incomplete fix of CVE-2026-25797 (bsc#1272579).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 15 SP6-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/ImageMagick&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2015%20SP6-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"ImageMagick":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-SUSE":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-limited":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-open":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-secure":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-websafe":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-devel":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","libMagick++-7_Q16HDRI5":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","libMagick++-devel":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","libMagickCore-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","libMagickWand-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","perl-PerlMagick":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4376-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server for SAP Applications 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/ImageMagick&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%20for%20SAP%20Applications%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"ImageMagick":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-SUSE":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-limited":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-open":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-secure":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream-websafe":"7.1.1.21-150600.3.87.1","Ima